<!-- SECTION 7: COMMON PATTERNS -->
<h1>7. Common Patterns &amp; Headers</h1>

<h3>Required Headers for ALL Requests</h3>
<pre>{
  "apikey": "{ANON_KEY}",
  "Content-Type": "application/json"
}

// For authenticated requests, add:
{
  "Authorization": "Bearer {jwt_access_token}"
}</pre>

<h3>PostgREST Query Operators</h3>
<table>
<tr><th>Operator</th><th>Usage</th><th>Example</th></tr>
<tr><td>eq</td><td>Equals</td><td><code>?company_id=eq.abc123</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>neq</td><td>Not equals</td><td><code>?status=neq.deleted</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>gt / gte</td><td>Greater than</td><td><code>?date=gte.2026-06-01</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>lt / lte</td><td>Less than</td><td><code>?date=lte.2026-08-31</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>like / ilike</td><td>Pattern match</td><td><code>?name=ilike.*john*</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>in</td><td>In list</td><td><code>?status=in.(active,pending)</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>is</td><td>IS NULL / IS TRUE</td><td><code>?checked_out_at=is.null</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>order</td><td>Sort results</td><td><code>?order=created_at.desc</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>limit</td><td>Limit results</td><td><code>?limit=50</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>offset</td><td>Pagination offset</td><td><code>?offset=50</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>select</td><td>Column selection</td><td><code>?select=id,name,email</code></td></tr>
</table>

<h3>Embedding Related Tables</h3>
<pre>// Get children with their bunk and division names
GET /rest/v1/children?select=*,bunks(bunk_name),divisions(name)&company_id=eq.{id}

// Get trips with attendees and staff
GET /rest/v1/trips?select=*,trip_attendees(children(name)),trip_staff(staff(name))&company_id=eq.{id}</pre>

<h3>Insert with Return</h3>
<pre>POST /rest/v1/children
Headers: { "Prefer": "return=representation" }
Body: { "name": "John Doe", "company_id": "...", "person_id": "..." }

// Returns the created record</pre>

<h3>Batch Insert</h3>
<pre>POST /rest/v1/trip_attendees
Body: [
  { "trip_id": "...", "child_id": "child1", "company_id": "..." },
  { "trip_id": "...", "child_id": "child2", "company_id": "..." }
]</pre>

<h3>Upsert</h3>
<pre>POST /rest/v1/daily_wolf_content
Headers: { "Prefer": "resolution=merge-duplicates" }
Body: { "company_id": "...", "date": "2026-07-15", "quote_of_the_day": "..." }</pre>

<h3>RPC (Database Functions)</h3>
<pre>POST /rest/v1/rpc/{function_name}
Body: { "param1": "value1" }</pre>

<h3>Authentication Flow for Mobile</h3>
<pre>
1. Sign Up:
   POST /auth/v1/signup
   Body: { "email": "user@camp.com", "password": "securePass123" }
   → Returns: { "access_token", "refresh_token", "user" }

2. Sign In:
   POST /auth/v1/token?grant_type=password
   Body: { "email": "user@camp.com", "password": "securePass123" }
   → Returns: { "access_token", "refresh_token", "user" }

3. Use token in all subsequent requests:
   Authorization: Bearer {access_token}

4. Refresh when expired:
   POST /auth/v1/token?grant_type=refresh_token
   Body: { "refresh_token": "..." }
   → Returns new { "access_token", "refresh_token" }

5. Sign Out:
   POST /auth/v1/logout
   Authorization: Bearer {access_token}
</pre>

<div class="warning">
<strong>Important Notes:</strong><br>
• All tables enforce Row Level Security (RLS) - users can only access data their role permits.<br>
• The default query limit is 1000 rows. Use <code>limit</code> and <code>offset</code> for pagination.<br>
• Always filter by <code>company_id</code> to scope data to the correct organization.<br>
• Season filtering (<code>season=eq.{season}</code>) is used across most modules.<br>
• Use Supabase client libraries (Swift, Kotlin, Flutter) for easier integration vs raw HTTP.
</div>

<hr class="section-divider">

<h1>27. Owl Pay (Canteen POS & Financials)</h1>

<p>Owl Pay is the point-of-sale canteen system with RFID scanning, balance management, and transaction tracking. Campers have pre-loaded balances that deduct on purchase; staff accumulate a running tab.</p>

<h2>27.1 Camper Balance</h2>
<p>The camper's Owl Pay balance is stored on the <code>children</code> table in the <code>owl_pay_balance</code> column (numeric, default 0).</p>

<h4>Get Camper Balance</h4>
<pre>
GET /rest/v1/children?select=id,name,owl_pay_balance,rfid,photo_url&company_id=eq.{company_id}&season=eq.{season}&status=neq.inactive&order=name
Authorization: Bearer {access_token}
apikey: {anon_key}
</pre>

<h4>Update Camper Balance (after purchase)</h4>
<pre>
PATCH /rest/v1/children?id=eq.{child_id}
Authorization: Bearer {access_token}
apikey: {anon_key}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "owl_pay_balance": 42.50 }
</pre>

<h2>27.2 Owl Pay Items</h2>
<p>Manage canteen items available for purchase.</p>

<table>
<tr><th>Column</th><th>Type</th><th>Required</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr>
<tr><td>id</td><td>uuid</td><td>Auto</td><td>gen_random_uuid()</td><td>Primary key</td></tr>
<tr><td>company_id</td><td>uuid</td><td>Yes</td><td>-</td><td>FK to companies</td></tr>
<tr><td>name</td><td>text</td><td>Yes</td><td>-</td><td>Item name</td></tr>
<tr><td>price</td><td>numeric</td><td>Yes</td><td>0</td><td>Item price</td></tr>
<tr><td>category</td><td>text</td><td>Yes</td><td>'snacks'</td><td>Category: food, snacks, drinks</td></tr>
<tr><td>active</td><td>boolean</td><td>Yes</td><td>true</td><td>Whether item is available</td></tr>
<tr><td>created_at</td><td>timestamptz</td><td>Auto</td><td>now()</td><td>Created timestamp</td></tr>
<tr><td>updated_at</td><td>timestamptz</td><td>Auto</td><td>now()</td><td>Updated timestamp</td></tr>
</table>

<h4>List Active Items</h4>
<pre>
GET /rest/v1/owl_pay_items?company_id=eq.{company_id}&active=eq.true&order=name
Authorization: Bearer {access_token}
apikey: {anon_key}
</pre>

<h4>Create Item</h4>
<pre>
POST /rest/v1/owl_pay_items
Authorization: Bearer {access_token}
apikey: {anon_key}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "company_id": "{company_id}",
  "name": "Ice Cream Sandwich",
  "price": 3.50,
  "category": "snacks"
}
</pre>

<h4>Update Item</h4>
<pre>
PATCH /rest/v1/owl_pay_items?id=eq.{item_id}
Authorization: Bearer {access_token}
apikey: {anon_key}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "price": 4.00, "active": false }
</pre>

<h2>27.3 Owl Pay Transactions (Ledger)</h2>
<p>Complete financial ledger of all purchases and free scans.</p>

<table>
<tr><th>Column</th><th>Type</th><th>Required</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr>
<tr><td>id</td><td>uuid</td><td>Auto</td><td>gen_random_uuid()</td><td>Primary key</td></tr>
<tr><td>company_id</td><td>uuid</td><td>Yes</td><td>-</td><td>FK to companies</td></tr>
<tr><td>child_id</td><td>uuid</td><td>No</td><td>null</td><td>FK to children (or staff id)</td></tr>
<tr><td>item_id</td><td>uuid</td><td>No</td><td>null</td><td>FK to owl_pay_items</td></tr>
<tr><td>amount</td><td>numeric</td><td>Yes</td><td>0</td><td>Transaction amount</td></tr>
<tr><td>is_free</td><td>boolean</td><td>Yes</td><td>false</td><td>Whether this was a free item</td></tr>
<tr><td>transaction_type</td><td>text</td><td>Yes</td><td>'purchase'</td><td>'purchase' or 'first_scan'</td></tr>
<tr><td>notes</td><td>text</td><td>No</td><td>null</td><td>Transaction notes</td></tr>
<tr><td>created_by</td><td>uuid</td><td>No</td><td>null</td><td>User who processed</td></tr>
<tr><td>created_at</td><td>timestamptz</td><td>Auto</td><td>now()</td><td>Transaction timestamp</td></tr>
</table>

<h4>List Transactions (with item details)</h4>
<pre>
GET /rest/v1/owl_pay_transactions?select=*,owl_pay_items(name,category)&company_id=eq.{company_id}&order=created_at.desc
Authorization: Bearer {access_token}
apikey: {anon_key}
</pre>

<h4>List Transactions for a Camper</h4>
<pre>
GET /rest/v1/owl_pay_transactions?child_id=eq.{child_id}&company_id=eq.{company_id}&order=created_at.desc
Authorization: Bearer {access_token}
apikey: {anon_key}
</pre>

<h4>Record Purchase Transaction</h4>
<pre>
POST /rest/v1/owl_pay_transactions
Authorization: Bearer {access_token}
apikey: {anon_key}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "company_id": "{company_id}",
  "child_id": "{child_id}",
  "item_id": "{item_id}",
  "amount": 3.50,
  "is_free": false,
  "transaction_type": "purchase",
  "created_by": "{user_id}"
}
</pre>

<h4>Record First Scan (Free Entry)</h4>
<pre>
POST /rest/v1/owl_pay_transactions
Authorization: Bearer {access_token}
apikey: {anon_key}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "company_id": "{company_id}",
  "child_id": "{child_id}",
  "amount": 0,
  "is_free": true,
  "transaction_type": "first_scan",
  "notes": "First scan of the day - free entry",
  "created_by": "{user_id}"
}
</pre>

<h2>27.4 Daily Scans (First Scan Tracking)</h2>
<p>Tracks whether a camper has already scanned today. Each camper gets one free item per day (resets daily). Staff do not receive free scans.</p>

<table>
<tr><th>Column</th><th>Type</th><th>Required</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr>
<tr><td>id</td><td>uuid</td><td>Auto</td><td>gen_random_uuid()</td><td>Primary key</td></tr>
<tr><td>company_id</td><td>uuid</td><td>Yes</td><td>-</td><td>FK to companies</td></tr>
<tr><td>child_id</td><td>uuid</td><td>Yes</td><td>-</td><td>FK to children</td></tr>
<tr><td>scan_date</td><td>date</td><td>Yes</td><td>CURRENT_DATE</td><td>Date of scan</td></tr>
<tr><td>created_at</td><td>timestamptz</td><td>Auto</td><td>now()</td><td>Created timestamp</td></tr>
</table>

<div class="note">
<strong>Unique Constraint:</strong> <code>(company_id, child_id, scan_date)</code> ensures only one daily scan record per camper per day.
</div>

<h4>Check if Camper Has Scanned Today</h4>
<pre>
GET /rest/v1/owl_pay_daily_scans?child_id=eq.{child_id}&scan_date=eq.{today}&select=id
Authorization: Bearer {access_token}
apikey: {anon_key}

→ Empty array = first scan (free item eligible)
→ Has record = already scanned today
</pre>

<h4>Record Daily Scan</h4>
<pre>
POST /rest/v1/owl_pay_daily_scans
Authorization: Bearer {access_token}
apikey: {anon_key}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "company_id": "{company_id}",
  "child_id": "{child_id}"
}
</pre>

<h2>27.5 Reporting Queries</h2>

<h4>Revenue by Date Range</h4>
<pre>
GET /rest/v1/owl_pay_transactions?company_id=eq.{company_id}&is_free=eq.false&created_at=gte.{start_date}&created_at=lte.{end_date}&select=amount,created_at
Authorization: Bearer {access_token}
apikey: {anon_key}
</pre>

<h4>Top Selling Items</h4>
<pre>
GET /rest/v1/owl_pay_transactions?company_id=eq.{company_id}&transaction_type=eq.purchase&select=item_id,owl_pay_items(name,category)&order=created_at.desc
Authorization: Bearer {access_token}
apikey: {anon_key}
</pre>

<h4>Low Balance Campers</h4>
<pre>
GET /rest/v1/children?company_id=eq.{company_id}&season=eq.{season}&owl_pay_balance=lt.5&status=neq.inactive&select=id,name,owl_pay_balance&order=owl_pay_balance
Authorization: Bearer {access_token}
apikey: {anon_key}
</pre>

<h2>27.6 RLS Policies</h2>
<div class="note">
<strong>Access Rules:</strong><br>
• <strong>owl_pay_items:</strong> Admin/staff can manage; all authenticated users in company can view.<br>
• <strong>owl_pay_transactions:</strong> Admin/staff can manage; all authenticated users in company can view.<br>
• <strong>owl_pay_daily_scans:</strong> Admin/staff can manage; all authenticated users in company can view.<br>
• <strong>children.owl_pay_balance:</strong> Follows existing children table RLS (admin/staff can update).<br>
• All tables are company-scoped via <code>get_user_company(auth.uid())</code>.
</div>

<h2>27.7 Business Logic Notes</h2>
<div class="warning">
<strong>Key Rules:</strong><br>
• <strong>First Scan Free:</strong> Each camper gets one free item per day. Check <code>owl_pay_daily_scans</code> before processing. Staff do NOT get free scans.<br>
• <strong>Camper Balance:</strong> Deducted from <code>children.owl_pay_balance</code> on purchase. Reject if insufficient funds.<br>
• <strong>Staff Tab:</strong> Staff purchases are recorded in transactions but do NOT deduct from a balance — they accumulate a running tab total.<br>
• <strong>RFID:</strong> Both <code>children.rfid</code> and <code>staff.rfid</code> fields are used for POS scanning. Check campers first, then staff.
</div>

</body>
</html>